      "link": null,
      "locked": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gBqcxGKutsVlPQoYZ9bP5",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10454.275992873914,
      "y": -5442.645962119923,
      "width": 1426.54345703125,
      "height": 910,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "9Vj8gs05MIkvVDhex_BEU"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0E",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1400862338,
      "version": 566,
      "versionNonce": 833392514,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1792756752707,
      "created": 1792751903296,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Phase 1: Inside Your PC (Building the Box)\n1. Creating the Ping (Layer 3 - OS):\n\nYou type ping 8.8.8.8.\n\nYour OS creates a tiny ICMP Echo Request payload and wraps it in an IP Packet:\n\nSource IP: 192.168.1.5 | Dest IP: 8.8.8.8\n\n2. The Routing Decision (Layer 3 - OS):\n\nYour OS compares 8.8.8.8 to your home network (192.168.1.x).\n\nIt realises 8.8.8.8 is outside your house, so the packet must go to your Default Gateway (192.168.1.1).\n\n3. Checking the ARP Cache (Layer 2 - OS RAM):\n\nYour OS checks its RAM for 192.168.1.1 and finds your router's inside MAC: BB:BB.\n\n4. Framing & Transmission (Layer 2 & 1 - NIC):\n\nYour OS wraps the IP Packet inside a Frame:\n\n[ Dest MAC: BB:BB ] [ Source MAC: AA:AA ] [ Source IP: 192.168.1.5 | Dest IP: 8.8.8.8 ]\n\nIt hands the frame to your Wi-Fi NIC, which blasts it out as radio waves.",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "m8ksAvB5jbyz-9dADzq09",
      "originalText": "Phase 1: Inside Your PC (Building the Box)\n1. Creating the Ping (Layer 3 - OS):\n\nYou type ping 8.8.8.8.\n\nYour OS creates a tiny ICMP Echo Request payload and wraps it in an IP Packet:\n\nSource IP: 192.168.1.5 | Dest IP: 8.8.8.8\n\n2. The Routing Decision (Layer 3 - OS):\n\nYour OS compares 8.8.8.8 to your home network (192.168.1.x).\n\nIt realises 8.8.8.8 is outside your house, so the packet must go to your Default Gateway (192.168.1.1).\n\n3. Checking the ARP Cache (Layer 2 - OS RAM):\n\nYour OS checks its RAM for 192.168.1.1 and finds your router's inside MAC: BB:BB.\n\n4. Framing & Transmission (Layer 2 & 1 - NIC):\n\nYour OS wraps the IP Packet inside a Frame:\n\n[ Dest MAC: BB:BB ] [ Source MAC: AA:AA ] [ Source IP: 192.168.1.5 | Dest IP: 8.8.8.8 ]\n\nIt hands the frame to your Wi-Fi NIC, which blasts it out as radio waves.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "zkVwDeF_AwSCZrxifT40b",
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": 10207.548369888074,
      "y": -4318.201560061003,
      "width": 1996.6667938232422,
      "height": 920,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "9Vj8gs05MIkvVDhex_BEU"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0F",
      "roundness": {
        "type": 3
      },
      "seed": 1712856990,
      "version": 1409,
      "versionNonce": 305352514,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "oBADzHhF2nsR5gUjgLej1"
        },
        {
          "id": "XVBUzf9XYkqdJV7XhrQnf",
          "type": "arrow"
        },
        {
          "id": "_TaB1soqlfkf9qsUCV0Me",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1792756752707,
      "created": 1792751947170,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false
    },
    {
      "id": "oBADzHhF2nsR5gUjgLej1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10234.772269729383,
      "y": -4295.701560061003,
      "width": 1942.218994140625,
      "height": 875,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "9Vj8gs05MIkvVDhex_BEU"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0G",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 369201758,
      "version": 517,
      "versionNonce": 2068584194,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1792756752707,
      "created": 1792751964744,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Phase 2: Hop 1 — Your Home Router (The Strip & Rewrite)\n5. Receiving the Frame:\n\nYour router’s Wi-Fi NIC sees Dest MAC: BB:BB, accepts the frame, verifies the FCS checksum, and places it in the router's RAM.\n\n6. Stripping the Outer Frame:\n\nThe router throws the Wi-Fi Frame (AA:AA and BB:BB) in the bin. It pulls out the bare IP Packet and reads Dest IP: 8.8.8.8.\n\n7. NAT — Network Address Translation (Crucial Step):\n\nBecause 192.168.1.5 is a private home IP that doesn't exist on the public internet, Google wouldn't know where to send the reply.\n\nYour router rewrites the Source IP on the packet to its own Public WAN IP (49.205.10.20) and makes a note in its RAM table: \"Ping #1 came\nfrom 192.168.1.5.\"\n\n8. Reframing for the ISP (Hop 2):\n\nThe router looks up the ISP router's IP (49.205.10.1) in its Outside ARP Cache and gets MAC DD:DD.\n\nIt wraps the packet in a brand-new Frame:\n\n[ Dest MAC: DD:DD ] [ Source MAC: CC:CC ] [ Source IP: 49.205.10.20 | Dest IP: 8.8.8.8 ]\n\nThe router's fibre NIC converts this into pulses of light down the fibre optic cable.",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "zkVwDeF_AwSCZrxifT40b",
      "originalText": "Phase 2: Hop 1 — Your Home Router (The Strip & Rewrite)\n5. Receiving the Frame:\n\nYour router’s Wi-Fi NIC sees Dest MAC: BB:BB, accepts the frame, verifies the FCS checksum, and places it in the router's RAM.\n\n6. Stripping the Outer Frame:\n\nThe router throws the Wi-Fi Frame (AA:AA and BB:BB) in the bin. It pulls out the bare IP Packet and reads Dest IP: 8.8.8.8.\n\n7. NAT — Network Address Translation (Crucial Step):\n\nBecause 192.168.1.5 is a private home IP that doesn't exist on the public internet, Google wouldn't know where to send the reply.\n\nYour router rewrites the Source IP on the packet to its own Public WAN IP (49.205.10.20) and makes a note in its RAM table: \"Ping #1 came from 192.168.1.5.\"\n\n8. Reframing for the ISP (Hop 2):\n\nThe router looks up the ISP router's IP (49.205.10.1) in its Outside ARP Cache and gets MAC DD:DD.\n\nIt wraps the packet in a brand-new Frame:\n\n[ Dest MAC: DD:DD ] [ Source MAC: CC:CC ] [ Source IP: 49.205.10.20 | Dest IP: 8.8.8.8 ]\n\nThe router's fibre NIC converts this into pulses of light down the fibre optic cable.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "yqx6ItmQCBcZQzqzOF6RP",
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": 10220.881652358778,
      "y": -3181.534842531706,
      "width": 1996.6667938232422,
      "height": 920,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "9Vj8gs05MIkvVDhex_BEU"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0H",
      "roundness": {
        "type": 3
      },
      "seed": 1508485250,
      "version": 1520,
      "versionNonce": 494266050,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "LK7y3XkRlEO9EPSW2wdb5"
        },
        {
          "id": "_TaB1soqlfkf9qsUCV0Me",
          "type": "arrow"
        },
        {
          "id": "zcIdMY8ESwbBKfVQcWq04",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1792756752707,
      "created": 1792751970013,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LK7y3XkRlEO9EPSW2wdb5",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10228.799643996961,
      "y": -2931.534842531706,
      "width": 1980.830810546875,
      "height": 420,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "9Vj8gs05MIkvVDhex_BEU"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0I",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 403083358,
      "version": 529,
      "versionNonce": 1095745154,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1792756752707,
      "created": 1792752040410,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Phase 3: Hops 2 to 6 — The Internet Backbone\n\n9. The Relay Race:\n\nAt Hop 2 (ISP Router), the NIC sees Dest MAC: DD:DD, strips the frame, looks at Dest IP: 8.8.8.8 in its routing table, checks its ARP cache\nfor Hop 3's MAC, wraps it in a new frame, and fires it to Hop 3.\n\n\nThis exact Strip Frame $\\rightarrow$ Check Dest IP $\\rightarrow$ Put New MAC Frame cycle repeats at Hop 3, 4, 5, and 6.\n\nNotice: The IP Packet (Source: 49.205.10.20, Dest: 8.8.8.8) stays untouched the entire way; only the outer MAC Frame changes at every single\nrouter.",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "yqx6ItmQCBcZQzqzOF6RP",
      "originalText": "Phase 3: Hops 2 to 6 — The Internet Backbone\n\n9. The Relay Race:\n\nAt Hop 2 (ISP Router), the NIC sees Dest MAC: DD:DD, strips the frame, looks at Dest IP: 8.8.8.8 in its routing table, checks its ARP cache for Hop 3's MAC, wraps it in a new frame, and fires it to Hop 3.\n\n\nThis exact Strip Frame $\\rightarrow$ Check Dest IP $\\rightarrow$ Put New MAC Frame cycle repeats at Hop 3, 4, 5, and 6.\n\nNotice: The IP Packet (Source: 49.205.10.20, Dest: 8.8.8.8) stays untouched the entire way; only the outer MAC Frame changes at every single router.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "T42y4i3ghmEAAvH8CpSB1",
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": 10262.548217300184,
      "y": -2002.3681250024092,
      "width": 1996.6667938232422,
      "height": 1025,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "9Vj8gs05MIkvVDhex_BEU"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0J",
      "roundness": {
        "type": 3
      },
      "seed": 793723970,
      "version": 1257,
      "versionNonce": 1134075458,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "4GzeyPYniV_YSiFwQHvcY"
        },
        {
          "id": "zcIdMY8ESwbBKfVQcWq04",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1792756752707,
      "created": 1792752101960,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false
    },
    {
      "id": "4GzeyPYniV_YSiFwQHvcY",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10270.03224897743,
      "y": -1997.3681250024092,
      "width": 1981.69873046875,
      "height": 1015,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "9Vj8gs05MIkvVDhex_BEU"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0K",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 408392450,
      "version": 515,
      "versionNonce": 288327170,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1792756752707,
      "created": 1792752117928,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Phase 4: Hop 7 — Google's Server & The Return Trip\n10. Arrival at Google:\n\nHop 6 puts Google's MAC (GG:GG) on the frame. Google's NIC accepts it, strips the frame, and hands the IP Packet to Google's OS.\n\n11. Creating the Reply:\n\nGoogle's OS sees the ICMP Ping Request, flips the addresses, and builds an ICMP Echo Reply packet:\n\nSource IP: 8.8.8.8 | Dest IP: 49.205.10.20 (Your router's public IP).\n\n12. Travelling Back (Hops 7 to 1):\n\nThe reply packet travels back through the routers (using each router's routing table and ARP cache hop-by-hop) until it hits your home router's\nfibre port.\n\n13. Reverse NAT & Final Delivery to Your PC:\n\nYour home router strips the ISP frame and sees the reply for Ping #1.\n\nIt checks its NAT table in RAM, remembers Ping #1 belonged to 192.168.1.5, and rewrites the packet's Dest IP back to 192.168.1.5.\n\nIt checks its Inside ARP Cache for 192.168.1.5, finds your PC's MAC (AA:AA), wraps the packet in a Wi-Fi frame (Dest MAC: AA:AA), and beams\nit over Wi-Fi.\n\n14. Screen Output:\n\nYour PC's NIC catches the frame, strips it, hands the IP packet to Windows via DMA/interrupt, and your terminal prints: Reply from 8.8.8.8:\ntime=8ms.",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "T42y4i3ghmEAAvH8CpSB1",
      "originalText": "Phase 4: Hop 7 — Google's Server & The Return Trip\n10. Arrival at Google:\n\nHop 6 puts Google's MAC (GG:GG) on the frame. Google's NIC accepts it, strips the frame, and hands the IP Packet to Google's OS.\n\n11. Creating the Reply:\n\nGoogle's OS sees the ICMP Ping Request, flips the addresses, and builds an ICMP Echo Reply packet:\n\nSource IP: 8.8.8.8 | Dest IP: 49.205.10.20 (Your router's public IP).\n\n12. Travelling Back (Hops 7 to 1):\n\nThe reply packet travels back through the routers (using each router's routing table and ARP cache hop-by-hop) until it hits your home router's fibre port.\n\n13. Reverse NAT & Final Delivery to Your PC:\n\nYour home router strips the ISP frame and sees the reply for Ping #1.\n\nIt checks its NAT table in RAM, remembers Ping #1 belonged to 192.168.1.5, and rewrites the packet's Dest IP back to 192.168.1.5.\n\nIt checks its Inside ARP Cache for 192.168.1.5, finds your PC's MAC (AA:AA), wraps the packet in a Wi-Fi frame (Dest MAC: AA:AA), and beams it over Wi-Fi.\n\n14. Screen Output:\n\nYour PC's NIC catches the frame, strips it, hands the IP packet to Windows via DMA/interrupt, and your terminal prints: Reply from 8.8.8.8: time=8ms.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
