    {
      "id": "6xADxTWNnxdziEVXdGsSj",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 12364.370513641446,
      "y": 4355.965786257553,
      "width": 862.7357177734375,
      "height": 420,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0sV",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2081352350,
      "version": 788,
      "versionNonce": 685779842,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1792756521785,
      "created": 1792754685735,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Router\n\nAn ISP (Internet Service Provider) router—often called an\nedge router or Provider Edge (PE) router—is an industrial-\ngrade, heavy-duty network appliance (made by companies like\nCisco, Juniper, or Nokia) designed to handle thousands of home\nnetworks simultaneously.\n\nThis router also does Carrier Grade NAT, similar to NAT by a\nhome router but at a much larger scale. It would remember the\nrouter a frame came from and replace the home router's\naddress with it's own edge router IP address",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "fbuFA4MlWHbmnvukyYBQ0",
      "originalText": "Router\n\nAn ISP (Internet Service Provider) router—often called an edge router or Provider Edge (PE) router—is an industrial-grade, heavy-duty network appliance (made by companies like Cisco, Juniper, or Nokia) designed to handle thousands of home networks simultaneously.\n\nThis router also does Carrier Grade NAT, similar to NAT by a home router but at a much larger scale. It would remember the router a frame came from and replace the home router's address with it's own edge router IP address",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "J8rVNBJ5Fh9LM40DtS-Fz",
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": 5102.832497458407,
      "y": -4628.796319775045,
      "width": 1080.0002034505214,
      "height": 646.6666666666665,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0u",
      "roundness": {
        "type": 3
      },
      "seed": 457949762,
      "version": 509,
      "versionNonce": 1023558594,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "52h914_yVH4dR_0dE_w_s"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1792755176162,
      "created": 1792754927623,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false
    },
    {
      "id": "52h914_yVH4dR_0dE_w_s",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5110.272967836011,
      "y": -4580.462986441711,
      "width": 1065.1192626953125,
      "height": 550,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "dotted",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0v",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1323182594,
      "version": 820,
      "versionNonce": 1229486978,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1792755176162,
      "created": 1792754927623,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Router\n\n1. IP Routing & Forwarding:\nThe OS looks at the Destination IP inside the packet, checks its routing table in RAM, and decides: \"Does\nthis packet need to go out the WAN fibre port to the internet, or does it stay inside the local LAN to\nanother device in the house?\"\n\n2. Network Address Translation (NAT):\nAs we covered, the software rewrites private local IP addresses into your single public WAN IP so your home\ndevices can share one internet connection.\n\n3. Firewall & Stateful Packet Inspection:\nThe OS maintains a tracking table of outbound connections. If an unsolicited packet arrives from the public\ninternet without a matching entry in that table, the OS software drops it to protect your home network.\n\n4. DHCP (Dynamic Host Configuration Protocol):\nThe software runs a background service that automatically hands out private IP addresses (192.168.1.x)\nwhenever a new phone or laptop connects to your Wi-Fi.\n\n5. DNS Forwarding / Caching:\nMost home router OS software acts as a local DNS proxy, caching domain lookups for your devices to speed\nup web browsing across the whole house.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "J8rVNBJ5Fh9LM40DtS-Fz",
      "originalText": "Router\n\n1. IP Routing & Forwarding:\nThe OS looks at the Destination IP inside the packet, checks its routing table in RAM, and decides: \"Does this packet need to go out the WAN fibre port to the internet, or does it stay inside the local LAN to another device in the house?\"\n\n2. Network Address Translation (NAT):\nAs we covered, the software rewrites private local IP addresses into your single public WAN IP so your home devices can share one internet connection.\n\n3. Firewall & Stateful Packet Inspection:\nThe OS maintains a tracking table of outbound connections. If an unsolicited packet arrives from the public internet without a matching entry in that table, the OS software drops it to protect your home network.\n\n4. DHCP (Dynamic Host Configuration Protocol):\nThe software runs a background service that automatically hands out private IP addresses (192.168.1.x) whenever a new phone or laptop connects to your Wi-Fi.\n\n5. DNS Forwarding / Caching:\nMost home router OS software acts as a local DNS proxy, caching domain lookups for your devices to speed up web browsing across the whole house.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
